        "comments": "The assembly bCyaCae1.hap2.1 is based on 80x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The microchromosomes were identified through second-shot curation of scaffolds smaller than 20 Mbp, combined with homology-based identification using known microchromosome genes via Microfinder.The Z chromosome was identified through synteny with Periparus ater (GCA_032357785.1).The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 2 (84,155 - 89,966 Kbp) are unknown.The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 3 (114,740 - 120,849 Kbp) are unknown. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 4 (63,032 - 73,687 Kbp) are unknown. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 5 (62,771 - 72,569 Kbp) are unknown.The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 6 (12,405 - 18,030 Kbp) are unknown.The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 7 (0 - 2,011 Kbp) are unknown.The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 8 (30,957 - 33,088 Kbp) are unknown. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 8 (8,568 - 10,728 Kbp) are unknown.The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 9 (12,517 - 15,832 Kbp) are unknown.The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 28 (1,192 - 7,774 Kbp) are unknown.The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 31 (931 - 3,911 Kbp) are unknown.",
